{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And he camped in the valley of Gerar.</b> For he did not wish to uproot his dwelling from the land of the Philistines entirely, because the command of the King, the King of all the world, is, namely (Genesis 26:3): ״גּוּר בָּאָרֶץ הַזֹּאת״. And even though it is said that that place was not included in what HaShem said to him, ״שְׁכֹן בָּאָרֶץ״, none the less he was compelled by the king, the lord of the land. Or perhaps HaShem did this as a test — for even though HaShem said to him, ״לְךָ וּלְזַרְעֲךָ אֶתֵּן אֶת כָּל הָאֲרָצוֹת״, none the less they did not let him dwell there even as one of the people, so that he would not speculate after the Shekhinah — and so He did to Abraham."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:43:34.073651671Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}